Tech stack and architecture for FinanzasDaniel v0.2 functional layer:

PERSISTENCE SPLIT
- UserDefaults (AppStorageKeys enum): monthlyIncome, payDay, onboardingComplete, suggestedVariableBudget, notificationsGranted
- SwiftData: SavingsGoal, Contribution, Expense, FixedExpense, MonthlySnapshot
- No Core Data. No third-party persistence.

NEW FILES TO CREATE (do not modify existing working UI files without instruction):
  AppState.swift                    — @Observable singleton
  NotificationScheduler.swift       — UNUserNotificationCenter wrapper + action handlers
  BudgetCalculator.swift            — Pure functions, zero side effects, fully testable
  MonthlySnapshot+AutoCreate.swift  — Logic for snapshot creation
  
  Onboarding/
    OnboardingFlow.swift            — Manages step state machine (enum Step)
    OnboardingWelcomeView.swift     — Step 0: splash
    OnboardingIncomeView.swift      — Step 1: income + pay day
    OnboardingFixedView.swift       — Step 2: fixed expenses
    OnboardingGoalsView.swift       — Step 3: goals
    OnboardingBudgetView.swift      — Step 4: budget reveal + notifications
    OnboardingPreset.swift          — Preset chips data (Icetex, Netflix, etc.)
  
  Components/
    HeroNumberInput.swift           — Large SF Mono input with $ prefix
    FixedExpenseRow.swift           — Inline editable row (name, amount, day)
    GoalEditorCard.swift            — Inline goal creator with emoji picker
    EmojiPickerGrid.swift           — 40-emoji grid, 8 columns
    StatsComparisonCard.swift       — Month vs month card with Canvas bar chart
    BudgetBreakdownCard.swift       — Read-only breakdown (onboarding step 4)
    NotificationPermissionCard.swift
    DeltaChip.swift                 — "↑12%" / "↓8%" chip with semantic color

ENTRY POINT LOGIC (FinanzasDanielApp.swift):
  On launch: check UserDefaults "onboarding_complete"
  false → OnboardingFlow (fullscreen, no tab bar)
  true  → MainTabView
  Use @AppStorage("onboarding_complete") for reactive binding.

STEP STATE MACHINE (OnboardingFlow):
  enum OnboardingStep: Int, CaseIterable {
    case welcome, income, fixed, goals, budget
  }
  @State var currentStep: OnboardingStep = .welcome
  Transition: .asymmetric(insertion: .move(edge: .trailing), removal: .move(edge: .leading))
  Progress: (currentStep.rawValue + 1) / OnboardingStep.allCases.count

NOTIFICATION CATEGORIES:
  UNNotificationCategory identifier: "FIXED_EXPENSE_REMINDER"
  Actions: "PAID" (title: "Sí, ya pagué"), "SNOOZE" (title: "Recordar mañana")
  Register category on app launch (before permission request).

SWIFTDATA QUERY PATTERNS:
  // Current month expenses — live
  @Query(filter: #Predicate<Expense> { expense in
    expense.date >= startOfMonth && expense.date <= endOfMonth
  }, sort: \.date, order: .reverse) var currentExpenses: [Expense]
  
  // Use Calendar.current for startOfMonth/endOfMonth computation
  // Wrap in ExpensesViewModel for testability

BUDGET CALCULATOR (pure, no side effects):
  struct BudgetCalculator {
    static func suggested(income: Double, fixed: [FixedExpense], goals: [SavingsGoal]) -> Double {
      let fixedTotal = fixed.filter(\.isActive).reduce(0) { $0 + $1.amount }
      let goalsTotal = goals.filter(\.isActive).reduce(0) { $0 + $1.monthlyContribution }
      let buffer = max(income * 0.10, 50_000)
      return max(income - fixedTotal - goalsTotal - buffer, 0)
    }
  }

DO NOT:
- Do not use async/await for UserDefaults reads (synchronous only)
- Do not schedule notifications in a View — only in NotificationScheduler
- Do not put business logic in SwiftUI body or computed vars on views
- Do not recreate ModelContainer in multiple places — one instance in App
